apabilitiesRequestPayload (Issue D) – **NEW CONTRADICTION**  \n     §3.7 defines empty interface “同 v1”, §7.2.1 adds `supportedProtocolVersions?: string[]`. This is a v2 self-consistency issue introduced by the new handshake flow.I found another subtle issue in Changelog item 1:\n**Summary**  \nI reviewed the D2 v2 schema against the D1 baseline and the two new self-consistency issues you flagged. The first (Changelog wording vs actual placement of `ts`) is a minor documentation slip that does not affect runtime behavior. The second (leftover v1 phrasing in §7 4) is a medium-low self-consistency gap that could cause confusion for implementers but does not break the handshake or wire mapping. Both are closed by the existing D1 clarifications and the explicit “kernelport/1” decision. Verdict: PASS_WITH_NOTE.\n\n**Files touched**  \n- `/Users/litian yi/.llm-wiki/agent-app-design/kernel/d2-message-schema-v2.md` (441 lines) – primary target; no edits made.\n\n**Acceptance verification (N/N)**  \n1. First-round findings closed  \n   - BLOCKER (protocolVersion + ts): D1 §2 and §7.1 still contain the unique `ts` location on EventEnvelope; D2 v2 preserves it.  \n   - protocolVersion literal scheme: D1 clarification comment (“不改语义”, design_status confirmed) matches v2 wording.The task is complete. I've written the adversarial review deliverable to T-016-output.md. I should give a brief summary of the verdict to the user (though this is a background dispatch, a short confir...",
